<!-- =====================================================================
     5-STEP CONTRIBUTOR GUIDE
     ===================================================================== -->
<section class="w-full bg-bg-2 dark:bg-bg-dark-2 bg-dots py-14 sm:py-18 md:py-22 border-b-2 border-border" id="guide">
  <div class="container-site">
    <div class="w-full text-center flex flex-col items-center justify-center max-w-3xl mx-auto mb-12 sm:mb-16">
      <div class="mb-4">
        <Badge Variant="primary"><span data-i18n="guide.badge">Onboarding Fast-Track</span></Badge>
      </div>
      <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl md:text-4xl font-black tracking-tight text-fg dark:text-fg-dark mb-4" data-i18n="guide.title">Start Contributing in 5 Steps</h2>
      <p class="text-sm sm:text-base text-muted dark:text-muted-dark leading-relaxed" data-i18n="guide.subtitle">From zero to your first merged pull request. Here is how to get your development environment running in minutes.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-6">
      <Card variant="default" class="p-6 bg-bg dark:bg-bg-dark" style="border:var(--pop-border); box-shadow:var(--pop-shadow)">
        <span class="inline-flex items-center justify-center w-8 h-8 rounded-lg bg-primary text-primary-content font-black text-sm mb-4">1</span>
        <h3 class="text-base font-extrabold text-fg dark:text-fg-dark mb-2" data-i18n="guide.s1_title">1. Fork &amp; Clone Repositories</h3>
        <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-muted dark:text-muted-dark leading-relaxed mb-3" data-i18n="guide.s1_desc">Fork any Krewire repository to your personal GitHub account, then clone it locally to begin:</p>
        <Terminal Command="git clone https://github.com/your-username/krewire && cd krewire" />
      </Card>

      <Card variant="default" class="p-6 bg-bg dark:bg-bg-dark" style="border:var(--pop-border); box-shadow:var(--pop-shadow)">
        <span class="inline-flex items-center justify-center w-8 h-8 rounded-lg bg-primary text-primary-content font-black text-sm mb-4">2</span>
        <h3 class="text-base font-extrabold text-fg dark:text-fg-dark mb-2" data-i18n="guide.s2_title">2. Build the kiw CLI from Source</h3>
        <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-muted dark:text-muted-dark leading-relaxed mb-3" data-i18n="guide.s2_desc">Inside your clone of the core repository (Go 1.27.1+), build the CLI you are changing:</p>
        <Terminal Command="go build -o bin/kiw ./tools/kiw/cmd/kiw && ./bin/kiw version" />
      </Card>

      <Card variant="default" class="p-6 bg-bg dark:bg-bg-dark" style="border:var(--pop-border); box-shadow:var(--pop-shadow)">
        <span class="inline-flex items-center justify-center w-8 h-8 rounded-lg bg-primary text-primary-content font-black text-sm mb-4">3</span>
        <h3 class="text-base font-extrabold text-fg dark:text-fg-dark mb-2" data-i18n="guide.s3_title">3. Pick an Open Issue</h3>
        <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-muted dark:text-muted-dark leading-relaxed mb-4" data-i18n-html="guide.s3_desc_html">Browse our curated issues list tagged with <span class="badge badge-primary text-2xs">good first issue</span> or <span class="badge badge-secondary text-2xs">help wanted</span>. Comment to let maintainers know you are working on it.</p>
        <Button Variant="outline" Size="sm" Href="https://github.com/krewire/krewire/issues?q=is%3Aissue+is%3Aopen+label%3A%22good+first+issue%22" DataI18n="guide.s3_btn">View Good First Issues →</Button>
      </Card>

      <Card variant="default" class="p-6 bg-bg dark:bg-bg-dark" style="border:var(--pop-border); box-shadow:var(--pop-shadow)">
        <span class="inline-flex items-center justify-center w-8 h-8 rounded-lg bg-primary text-primary-content font-black text-sm mb-4">4</span>
        <h3 class="text-base font-extrabold text-fg dark:text-fg-dark mb-2" data-i18n="guide.s4_title">4. Implement &amp; Verify Locally</h3>
        <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-muted dark:text-muted-dark leading-relaxed mb-3" data-i18n="guide.s4_desc">Write clean, idiomatic Go code and tests. Run the quality gates from CONTRIBUTING.md before opening a pull request:</p>
        <Terminal Command="gofmt -l . && go vet ./... && go test ./..." />
      </Card>

      <Card variant="default" class="p-6 bg-bg dark:bg-bg-dark" style="border:var(--pop-border); box-shadow:var(--pop-shadow)">
        <span class="inline-flex items-center justify-center w-8 h-8 rounded-lg bg-primary text-primary-content font-black text-sm mb-4">5</span>
        <h3 class="text-base font-extrabold text-fg dark:text-fg-dark mb-2" data-i18n="guide.s5_title">5. Submit PR with Conventional Commits</h3>
        <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-muted dark:text-muted-dark leading-relaxed mb-3" data-i18n="guide.s5_desc">Open a PR following Conventional Commits (feat, fix, docs, refactor, test). Maintainers and AI Boost will review and guide you to merge.</p>
        <Terminal Command="git commit -m &quot;feat(web): add handler (ref #123)&quot;" />
      </Card>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- =====================================================================
     3 QUALITY GATES
     ===================================================================== -->
<section class="w-full bg-bg dark:bg-bg-dark bg-dots py-14 sm:py-18 md:py-22 border-b-2 border-border" id="standards">
  <div class="container-site">
    <div class="w-full text-center flex flex-col items-center justify-center max-w-3xl mx-auto mb-12 sm:mb-16">
      <div class="mb-4">
        <Badge Variant="primary"><span data-i18n="standards.badge">Quality Assurance</span></Badge>
      </div>
      <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl md:text-4xl font-black tracking-tight text-fg dark:text-fg-dark mb-4" data-i18n="standards.title">The Krewire Way: 3 Quality Gates</h2>
      <p class="text-sm sm:text-base text-muted dark:text-muted-dark leading-relaxed" data-i18n="standards.subtitle">To keep the codebase reliable, predictable, and production-ready, every pull request must pass three gates. The canonical list lives in the core repository's CONTRIBUTING.md.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-6">
      <Card variant="default" class="p-6 bg-bg-2 dark:bg-bg-dark-2" style="border:var(--pop-border); box-shadow:var(--pop-shadow)">
        <div class="text-3xl mb-3">✓</div>
        <h3 class="text-base font-black text-fg dark:text-fg-dark mb-2" data-i18n="standards.gate1_title">Gate 1: Format &amp; Lint</h3>
        <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-muted dark:text-muted-dark leading-relaxed mb-4" data-i18n="standards.gate1_desc">Zero lint errors and idiomatic Go formatting. Code must adhere strictly to Go standard conventions.</p>
        <div class="p-3 rounded-lg bg-bg dark:bg-bg-dark border border-border-subtle text-xs font-mono font-bold text-primary" data-i18n="standards.gate1_req">Required: gofmt -l . (clean), go vet ./... (clean)</div>
      </Card>

      <Card variant="default" class="p-6 bg-bg-2 dark:bg-bg-dark-2" style="border:var(--pop-border); box-shadow:var(--pop-shadow)">
        <div class="text-3xl mb-3">🛡️</div>
        <h3 class="text-base font-black text-fg dark:text-fg-dark mb-2" data-i18n="standards.gate2_title">Gate 2: Tests</h3>
        <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-muted dark:text-muted-dark leading-relaxed mb-4" data-i18n="standards.gate2_desc">Every change must pass the module's unit and integration tests, and kiw compat must report ok after version.go changes.</p>
        <div class="p-3 rounded-lg bg-bg dark:bg-bg-dark border border-border-subtle text-xs font-mono font-bold text-primary" data-i18n="standards.gate2_req">Required: go test ./... passes, kiw compat prints ok</div>
      </Card>

      <Card variant="default" class="p-6 bg-bg-2 dark:bg-bg-dark-2" style="border:var(--pop-border); box-shadow:var(--pop-shadow)">
        <div class="text-3xl mb-3">📝</div>
        <h3 class="text-base font-black text-fg dark:text-fg-dark mb-2" data-i18n="standards.gate3_title">Gate 3: Spec &amp; Commits</h3>
        <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-muted dark:text-muted-dark leading-relaxed mb-4" data-i18n="standards.gate3_desc">Changes must link to a valid Spec or Issue, following Conventional Commits format.</p>
        <div class="p-3 rounded-lg bg-bg dark:bg-bg-dark border border-border-subtle text-xs font-mono font-bold text-primary" data-i18n="standards.gate3_req">Required: Semantic commit format &amp; spec traceability</div>
      </Card>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- =====================================================================
     PUBLIC GOVERNANCE & RFC FRAMEWORK
     ===================================================================== -->
<section class="w-full bg-bg-2 dark:bg-bg-dark-2 bg-dots py-14 sm:py-18 md:py-22 border-b-2 border-border" id="governance">
  <div class="container-site">
    <div class="w-full text-center flex flex-col items-center justify-center max-w-3xl mx-auto mb-12 sm:mb-16">
      <div class="mb-4">
        <Badge Variant="secondary">Ecosystem Governance</Badge>
      </div>
      <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl md:text-4xl font-black tracking-tight text-fg dark:text-fg-dark mb-4">Public RFC Workflow &amp; Architectural Decisions</h2>
      <p class="text-sm sm:text-base text-muted dark:text-muted-dark leading-relaxed">Krewire operates under transparent open-source governance. All major architectural shifts follow the Request for Comments (RFC) process before becoming permanent Architectural Decision Records (ADRs).</p>
    </div>

    <!-- 4-Phase RFC Process -->
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4 gap-6 mb-12">
      <Card variant="default" class="p-6 bg-bg dark:bg-bg-dark" style="border:var(--pop-border); box-shadow:var(--pop-shadow)">
        <div class="text-xs font-black uppercase tracking-wider text-primary mb-2 font-mono">Phase 1</div>
        <h3 class="font-extrabold text-base text-fg dark:text-fg-dark mb-2">Proposal &amp; Problem</h3>
        <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-muted dark:text-muted-dark leading-relaxed">Open a GitHub Discussion in <code>krewire/internal</code> outlining the motivation, trade-offs, and ecosystem impact.</p>
      </Card>

      <Card variant="default" class="p-6 bg-bg dark:bg-bg-dark" style="border:var(--pop-border); box-shadow:var(--pop-shadow)">
        <div class="text-xs font-black uppercase tracking-wider text-primary mb-2 font-mono">Phase 2</div>
        <h3 class="font-extrabold text-base text-fg dark:text-fg-dark mb-2">Formal RFC Draft</h3>
        <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-muted dark:text-muted-dark leading-relaxed">Submit an RFC PR using the standard template covering API design, failure modes, and migration plans.</p>
      </Card>

      <Card variant="default" class="p-6 bg-bg dark:bg-bg-dark" style="border:var(--pop-border); box-shadow:var(--pop-shadow)">
        <div class="text-xs font-black uppercase tracking-wider text-primary mb-2 font-mono">Phase 3</div>
        <h3 class="font-extrabold text-base text-fg dark:text-fg-dark mb-2">14-Day Review</h3>
        <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-muted dark:text-muted-dark leading-relaxed">Public comment period for Indonesian and global contributors to review, benchmark, and propose refinements.</p>
      </Card>

      <Card variant="default" class="p-6 bg-bg dark:bg-bg-dark" style="border:var(--pop-border); box-shadow:var(--pop-shadow-lg)">
        <div class="text-xs font-black uppercase tracking-wider text-primary mb-2 font-mono">Phase 4</div>
        <h3 class="font-extrabold text-base text-fg dark:text-fg-dark mb-2">Consensus &amp; ADR</h3>
        <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-muted dark:text-muted-dark leading-relaxed">Consensus among Maintainers promotes the RFC into an immutable ADR (e.g., ADR-6CAB8C) committed to <code>internal/</code>.</p>
      </Card>
    </div>

    <!-- Public ADR Digest -->
    <Card variant="default" class="p-6 sm:p-8 bg-bg dark:bg-bg-dark mb-10" style="border:var(--pop-border); box-shadow:var(--pop-shadow)">
      <h3 class="font-black text-lg text-fg dark:text-fg-dark mb-5">Canonical Architectural Decision Records (ADR Digest)</h3>
      <div class="flex flex-col gap-4">
        <div class="p-4 rounded-xl border border-border-subtle bg-bg-2 dark:bg-bg-dark-2">
          <span class="font-mono font-bold text-primary">ADR-6CAB8C</span>: <strong class="text-fg dark:text-fg-dark">Ecosystem Architecture Baseline &amp; Strict Downward-Only Dependencies</strong>
          <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-muted dark:text-muted-dark mt-1">Defines strict unidirectional boundaries: <code>templates/boost → tools/kiw → pkg/* → pkg/model</code>. Zero upward edges allowed.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="p-4 rounded-xl border border-border-subtle bg-bg-2 dark:bg-bg-dark-2">
          <span class="font-mono font-bold text-primary">ADR-C9L2P</span>: <strong class="text-fg dark:text-fg-dark">Multi-Workload Single Binary Dispatch</strong>
          <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-muted dark:text-muted-dark mt-1">Standardizes 8 workload kinds behind <code>krewire.yaml</code> and unified CLI <code>kiw</code> with zero framework lock-in.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="p-4 rounded-xl border border-border-subtle bg-bg-2 dark:bg-bg-dark-2">
          <span class="font-mono font-bold text-primary">ADR-D1F3N</span>: <strong class="text-fg dark:text-fg-dark">Zero-Trust Defense-in-Depth Edge Security</strong>
          <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-muted dark:text-muted-dark mt-1">Requires CSRF token verification, ACME automated TLS, token bucket rate limiting, and secure HTTP response headers across all daemons.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </Card>

    <!-- Code of Conduct & Security Reporting -->
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
      <Card variant="default" class="p-6 bg-bg dark:bg-bg-dark" style="border:var(--pop-border); box-shadow:var(--pop-shadow)">
        <h4 class="font-extrabold text-base text-fg dark:text-fg-dark mb-2">📜 Contributor Covenant Code of Conduct (v2.1)</h4>
        <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-muted dark:text-muted-dark mb-4 leading-relaxed">We pledge to make participation in Krewire a harassment-free experience for everyone, regardless of age, body size, visible or invisible disability, ethnicity, sex characteristics, gender identity, or experience level.</p>
        <a href="https://github.com/krewire/.github/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-xs font-bold text-primary hover:underline">Read Full Code of Conduct (EN/ID) →</a>
      </Card>
      <Card variant="default" class="p-6 bg-bg dark:bg-bg-dark" style="border:var(--pop-border); box-shadow:var(--pop-shadow)">
        <h4 class="font-extrabold text-base text-fg dark:text-fg-dark mb-2">🔒 Security Vulnerability Reporting</h4>
        <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-muted dark:text-muted-dark mb-4 leading-relaxed">Never open a public issue for suspected security vulnerabilities. Please report any potential vulnerability responsibly via our encrypted reporting channel.</p>
        <p class="text-xs font-mono font-bold text-primary">security@krewire.com (PGP key in internal/docs/security/)</p>
      </Card>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

